  iter-71 EMERGENCY FIX: Proper adaptive-icon definition for the release variant.

  Background: @color/ic_launcher_background (white, #FFFFFFFF).
  Foreground: @drawable/ic_launcher_foreground — a 108dp vector with the
              "Y" glyph centered in the 72dp safe zone. Using a drawable
              (not a mipmap) is required so the adaptive-icon system can
              scale the layer at runtime without blurring a raster.
  Monochrome: same drawable — Android 13+ themes the layer with a single
              system color; must be a vector, not a raster.

  Root cause that this fixes (iter-71 postmortem):
    iter-59 used @mipmap/ic_launcher (a per-density PNG) as both the
    foreground and monochrome layers. On API 26+ the launcher clips the
    foreground to a mask shape; the PNG foreground was full-bleed and got
    clipped at the edges, making the icon appear misshapen or invisible
    depending on the device launcher. The monochrome PNG violated the
    Android 13 API contract (must be a single-color vector).
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
    <monochrome android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
